  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated WASH humanitarian response to support the most vulnerable Internally</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in Ethiopia will work to address the major Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) gaps by implementing WASH focused interventions that will improve supply of clean water to the target communities,  personal and environmental hygiene, rehabilitations of communal and institutional sanitation facilities enabling Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) access to dignified sanitation services. Maintenance and rehabilitation of water schemes including solarization of water systems, motorized pumps, hand pumps and springs are considered in the case of water supply. Maintenance of sanitation facilities, decommissioning of these that pose risks to the public, desludging of filled latrines will be carried out. In the case of hygiene promotion Oxfam will provide households with WASH, Non Food Items (NFI), Menstrual Hygiene Management (MHM) kits, environmental cleaning kits supported by community hygiene promotors/volunteers. Though the focus will be mainly in IDP camps host communities will also benefit from the intervention.</narrative>
  </description>
